sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Trader
    participant CD as CyberDeltaEngine
    participant ML as ML Module (Inactive)
    participant FRS as Funding Rate Strategy
    participant BP as Backpack API (CEX)
    participant HL as Hyperliquid API (DEX)
    participant PX as Paradex API (DEX)
    participant RM as Risk Management

    Note over CD,RM: Initialization Phase
    User->>CD: Initialize trading bot (Funding Rate Strategy Only)
    CD->>FRS: Initialize funding rate parameters (e.g., \\lambda for Utility)
    CD->>RM: Set base risk limits (VaR0, CVaR, max position)
    Note right of RM: Dynamic limits (VaR_t = f(\\sigma_mkt)) will be used in checks
    CD->>ML: Models loaded but inactive

    Note over CD,PX: Data Collection & Validation Phase
    loop Collect Market Data
        par Fetch CEX Data
            CD->>BP: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle data, depth
            BP-->>CD: Backpack Market Data
        and Fetch DEX Data (Hyperliquid)
            CD->>HL: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data, depth
            HL-->>CD: Hyperliquid Market Data
        and Fetch DEX Data (Paradex)
            CD->>PX: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data, depth
            PX-->>CD: Paradex Market Data
        end
        CD->>CD: Validate Data (Timestamps, Price Deviations, **vs Oracle**)
        Note right of CD: Handle validation failures (e.g., pause pair, log error)
    end

    Note over CD,RM: Analysis Phase
    CD->>FRS: Process validated funding rate data (BP, HL, PX)
    FRS->>FRS: Calculate basis volatility (\\sigma_B,t) per exchange/pair
    FRS->>FRS: Compute Expected Profit \\pi^X (incl. C^X)
    FRS->>FRS: Compute Expected Profit \\pi^{AB} (incl. C^{AB} - cost-adj. NFD)
    FRS->>FRS: **Calculate Utility U = \\pi_{adj} - \\lambda \\sigma_{B,t}^2**
    FRS-->>CD: Funding arbitrage signals (Utility U, Expected Profit, Volatility)
    Note right of FRS: ML E[FR] prediction bypassed

    CD->>RM: Calculate Kelly sizing based on signals (\\pi, \\sigma)
    RM->>RM: Apply fractional Kelly (\\alpha * f*) -> f_constrained
    RM->>RM: **Calculate current market vol \\sigma_{mkt,t}**
    RM->>RM: **Calculate dynamic limit VaR_t = VaR0 * (\\sigma_{mkt,t} / \\sigma_{mkt,0})**
    RM->>RM: Check portfolio risk constraints (\\sqrt{w^T \\Sigma w} <= MaxRisk, **PortfolioVaR <= VaR_t**)
    RM-->>CD: Position sizing recommendations (w_target)
    CD->>CD: Rank opportunities by **descending Utility U**

    Note over CD,RM: Collateral Check / Rebalancing Phase
    RM->>BP: Check current margin/collateral C_current^BP vs C_target^BP
    RM->>HL: Check current margin/collateral C_current^HL vs C_target^HL
    RM->>PX: Check current margin/collateral C_current^PX vs C_target^PX
    alt Collateral outside buffer or trade needs transfer
        RM->>RM: Trigger **detailed** collateral mgmt flow (dynamic paths, bridges...)
        Note right of RM: See cross_exchange_transfer_flow.mermaid for details
        RM->>BP: Initiate Transfers (if needed)
        RM->>HL: Initiate Transfers (if needed)
        RM->>PX: Initiate Transfers (if needed)
        BP-->>RM: Transfer Status
        HL-->>RM: Transfer Status
        PX-->>RM: Transfer Status
    end

    Note over CD,User: Decision & Execution Phase
    CD->>CD: Select highest ranked valid opportunity based on **Utility U**
    Note right of CD: Execution is latency-aware
    alt Single-Exchange Funding Arbitrage (e.g., on HL)
        CD->>HL: Execute delta-neutral position (e.g., Long Perp + Short Spot/Hedge)
        Note over CD,HL: Capturing HL funding rate
    else Cross-Exchange Arbitrage (e.g., BP vs HL)
        CD->>BP: Execute Leg 1 (e.g., Short Perp)
        CD->>HL: Execute Leg 2 (e.g., Long Perp, using IOC/FOK)
        Note over CD,HL: Exploiting BP vs HL funding differential
    else Cross-Exchange Arbitrage (e.g., HL vs PX)
        CD->>HL: Execute Leg 1
        CD->>PX: Execute Leg 2
        Note over CD,PX: Exploiting HL vs PX funding differential
    else Cross-Exchange Arbitrage (e.g., BP vs PX)
        CD->>BP: Execute Leg 1
        CD->>PX: Execute Leg 2
        Note over CD,PX: Exploiting BP vs PX funding differential
    end

    CD->>RM: Update open positions across all exchanges
    RM->>RM: Calculate real-time risk metrics (**PortfolioVaR vs VaR_t**, CVaR, \\sigma_P)

    Note over CD,User: Monitoring & Adaptation
    loop Every funding period (per exchange)
        par Collect BP Funding
            CD->>BP: Check/Receive funding payments
            BP-->>CD: Funding settlement info
        and Collect HL Funding
            CD->>HL: Check/Receive funding payments
            HL-->>CD: Funding settlement info
        and Collect PX Funding
            CD->>PX: Check/Receive funding payments
            PX-->>CD: Funding settlement info
        end
        CD->>CD: Update PnL and Funding Yield (FY)
    end

    loop Continuous Adaptation
        CD->>FRS: Update basis volatility estimates (\\sigma_B,t), costs, \\Sigma
        FRS-->>CD: Refreshed estimates
        CD->>RM: Re-evaluate position sizing / risk / collateral needs
        Note right of RM: **Performance trigger (e.g., Sharpe < Thresh) may adjust params (e.g., Kelly \\alpha)**
    end

    CD->>User: Performance Metrics (PnL, FY, Risk Exposure \\sigma_P/VaR_t)